{#
  Public as well as LAN, which is the default the macro already applies — so no `public=`
  argument here.

  The link a session emits is the ONE way anyone reaches an artifact, and a link that
  resolves only from inside the LAN fails wherever the reader actually is.

  A LAN-only route would also fail on login. Authelia selects its portal by the request's
  domain (see the `cookies:` list in roles/k8s/authelia — `auth.local.<domain>` for the LAN
  name, `auth.<domain>` for the public one), so a LAN-only route can only ever send a login
  through the LAN portal. Where that portal is unreachable the page hangs on the redirect and
  the service looks broken while it is serving fine.

  What still gates it: the `authelia` middleware, unchanged, on both names.
#}
---
{{ ingressroute(
    container_item.name,
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
    container_item.use_authelia,
  )
}}
